# fifo_stamp_publish_in_order: Stamps publish in command order: behind a faulted head, three NOPs complete but publish nothing; 0x1024 then publishes the last of them in one interrupt. A second faulted command behind the first faults again as soon as the first is resumed: the stamp before it is published (one interrupt), then its fault interrupt, with 0x103c at its offset.
{"op": "config", "ram": [["0x40000000", "0x4000000"]], "stamp_gpa": "0x40008000", "stamp_slots": 1, "watchdog_s": 30}
{"off": "0x1034", "op": "mmio_w", "val": "0xf5"}
{"off": "0x101c", "op": "mmio_w", "val": "0x10001"}
